== Third-party attribution ==

The `plugins/shunt-agy` plugin is an independent adaptation of Spotify's
"shunt" plugin, originally published at:

  https://github.com/spotify/portal-ai-plugins/tree/main/plugins/shunt

and described in the Spotify Engineering blog post:

  https://engineering.atspotify.com/2026/9/portal-by-spotify-cut-my-claude-code-token-usage-by-90

The original `shunt` is Copyright Spotify AB, licensed under the Apache
License, Version 2.0. shunt-agy retains the same three-layer design (hooks
that block large reads, scripts that delegate to a worker model, skills
that teach Claude when to call them) and, in several files, closely follows
the structure and wording of the original hooks and scripts.

Changes made in this derivative work:
  - The delegation target was changed from Spotify's internal Portal CLI /
    AiKA mode registry to the publicly available `agy` (Antigravity) CLI
    from Google, so the plugin works for anyone with `agy` installed
    instead of requiring access to Spotify's internal platform.
  - `scripts/lib/aika.sh` was replaced with `scripts/lib/worker.sh`, using
    agy's `stream-json` headless input/output protocol instead of the
    Portal CLI's `aika:invoke-chat` action.
  - `hooks/check-file-size` and `hooks/check-bash-read` also differ in
    behavior: they emit Claude Code's `hookSpecificOutput` permission
    format, also block by byte size (`SHUNT_MAX_BYTES`), and the Read hook
    lets binary files through. `scripts/code-write` and `scripts/bulk-read`
    reject flags without a value, and `code-write` strips only a markdown
    fence wrapped around the whole answer.
  - Benchmark fixtures under `plugins/shunt-agy/evals/fixtures/` were
    copied verbatim from the original repository (same license) to keep
    the token-savings measurements comparable.

The `modernize`, `takeover` and `leaving-pr-comments` skills in `plugins/desustack` are adapted from Theo Browne's "tstack",
https://github.com/t3dotgg/tstack, MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Theo Browne (full text: plugins/desustack/LICENSE-tstack).
Changes: `takeover` no longer depends on tstack's `file-pr` and `babysit-pr`,
`modernize` no longer authorizes pushing, and `leaving-pr-comments` states that
it never authorizes posting.

The `unslop`, `typescript-best-practices`, `blast-radius`, `correct`, `create-verification-skill`,
`figure-it-out`, `in-your-own-words`, `show-me-your-work` and `principle-*` skills in `plugins/desustack`
are adapted from Lauren Tan's "pstack", https://github.com/cursor/plugins/tree/main/pstack,
MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Lauren Tan (full text: plugins/desustack/LICENSE-pstack).
Changes: Cursor-specific paths and tools were replaced with Claude Code equivalents
(`.claude/skills`, the Agent tool with `isolation: "worktree"`, the session `transcript_path`),
`disable-model-invocation` was removed from some skills, and the descriptions of `unslop` and
`principle-fix-root-causes` were reworded. The `principles` skill, the hooks and the `Explore` agent
in `plugins/desustack` are original to this repository.

